# Code size hard caps

Enforce these limits on **new and edited** code. If a change would push a file over a hard cap, split first. Do not expand already-oversized files without extracting.

## Caps (lines)

| Codebase | Soft prefer | Hard max | Function / method hard max |
|---|---|---|---|
| iOS Swift (`apps/ios/**/*.swift`) | 250 | **400** | **50** |
| Android Kotlin (`apps/android/**/*.kt`) | 250 | **400** | **50** |
| Rust server (`server/**/*.rs`) | 250 | **400** | **50** |
| Dashboard Vue/TS (`apps/dashboard/src/**/*.{vue,ts}`) | 150 | **300** | **40** |

Count physical lines (including blanks/comments). Nested helpers inside a function count toward that function.

## Soft vs hard

- **Soft**: Prefer splitting when crossed (extract view/composable/module/helper).
- **Hard**: Must split before merging more logic. Agent must not add net lines past hard max.

## Exempt

- Generated code (`**/build/**`, `**/generated/**`, `**/dist/**`, KSP/Hilt outputs)
- Vendor / shadcn UI copies under `apps/dashboard/src/components/ui/**` (do not grow further; wrap instead)
- SQL migrations, lockfiles, asset catalogs, proto/schema dumps
- One-off data tables (e.g. large static enum maps) — still prefer split by domain

## Shared principles

- One primary type / screen / route module per file when practical
- Prefer many small pure helpers over one god function
- Extract when a function has >3 responsibilities or deeply nested control flow (>3 levels)
- New files should start under the soft prefer target
